==========================================
DAY 21 NOTES — Firewall Basics (ufw)
Date: 19-09-2026
==========================================

WHAT I LEARNED TODAY:
- Firewalls decide, rule by rule, what network traffic gets allowed or blocked
- "Default deny" (block everything, allow only what's needed) is the security-conscious approach
- ufw allow ssh MUST happen BEFORE ufw enable on a remote server — else instant lockout!
- ufw allow works by service name (ssh) or port number (22) — both work the same
- ufw deny <port> adds a blocking rule; ufw delete allow <port> removes a previous allow rule (different things!)
- ufw allow from <subnet> to any port <port> restricts access to a specific network range
- ufw logging on lets you see blocked attempts in /var/log/ufw.log

COMMANDS I PRACTICED:
[ ] ufw status / status verbose
[ ] ufw allow ssh (BEFORE enabling)
[ ] ufw enable
[ ] ufw allow <port> / ufw deny <port>
[ ] ufw delete allow <port>
[ ] ufw logging on

fill this in after running commands yourself :
$ sudo ufw status verbose
> 

$ sudo ufw allow ssh && sudo ufw enable
> 

$ sudo ufw allow 80 && sudo ufw status
> 


